      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"perfect child\" image was a performance, and you're tired of the act; it's exhausting to keep up a facade that isn't real. The peace you're seeking isn't a temporary pause; it's the quiet relief of finally stopping the fight against yourself. You don't have to keep proving your worth to anyone, especially not to ghosts of expectations. Just let the pressure lift, because the only way to truly stop feeling pathetic is to stop trying to be perfect.",
